tmp/

# Go build and test output
#
# `verse` is the binary name used by render.yaml, .github/workflows/ci.yml and the Dockerfile
# (`-o verse`). It was previously unignored, so a local build showed up in git status.
/verse

# `migrate` is the migration runner's build-output name, used the same way (`-o migrate`). It
# arrives with the versioned migration runner, which made the service depend on migrations having
# been applied before it starts.
#
# `migrations/` is the SQL and is tracked. These two are easy to confuse, and a pattern that matched
# both would silently stop the schema from being committed.
/migrate
*.test
coverage.out
vendor/

# server runtime
#
# Already listed in .dockerignore; named here so a local run does not leave them in the working
# tree. The pre-v0.3.7 CI wrote both; ad-hoc local runs still do.
server.log
server.pid
*.log
